  "body": "### Summary\n\nTwo filters asked for in #593 (item 4: \"read or unread\", flag kinds, \"anything else HFR offers\") have no single HFR request behind them. Before any code, the operator chooses how to offer them. Split from #593 (operator, 2026-11-13).\n\n### Questions for the operator\n1. **Unread-only, and flag combinations** (e.g. favourites + blue flags): HFR's `owntopic` has only 0 all, 1 tracked, 2 read, 3 favourites (HFR-PROTOCOL R2 row). Options:\n   - **(a) REST flag buckets.**\n     - What is known (#830, PR #872): `is_read`, `flag_owntopic` and the resume point per topic. The flat bucket of a category lists every flagged topic; the global one only those with news.\n     - Cost: one request per bucket, and buckets have no paging. They cover flagged topics only, not the whole category.\n   - **(b) Filter in the app over the loaded page.**\n     - Cost: rows of other pages stay hidden, so a \"filtered\" page may show few or no rows.\n   - **(c) Not offered**: keep Tous / Favoris / Suivis / Lus.\n2. **A picker on the Drapeaux and Favoris lists** (`forum1f.php`): their filter today is the favourites mode (`owntopic` 1 or 3, settings). `owntopic=2` is captured there (`R603e`); `owntopic=0` is a run observation only. Do you want a picker on these lists at all, and with which values?\n\n### After the decision\nThe chosen option gets a `ready` issue with its spec. Legacy at `87fe0d1c` has none of these filters, so this is a deliberate difference to record (ledger).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
